    "reasoning": "All 16 final answers agree with their own captured Math Academy solutions. The batch contains intermediate source errors: q-104516 writes -4x²+40x-116 during division, which should be -4x²-40x-116; q-128008 writes -i+3j-3j, which should be -i+3j-3k; q-120911 writes x_new=2+1=2 in Step 2, which should be 1+1=2. These errors do not change the final answers. Mathematical verification: q-122424 integrates velocity to r(t)=⟨3t²-t-14,t³/3-t-7⟩, giving r(1)=⟨-12,-23/3⟩. q-122471 integrates acceleration to v(t)=⟨1/t,-1⟩ and then obtains r(t)=⟨2+ln(t),4-t⟩. q-7221 similarly gives r(t)=⟨t³-t²,2t²-2⟩. q-104487 expands 3(x+5)(x²+9). q-104500 factors as (x+1/4)(36x²+4), giving remaining roots ±i/3. q-17409 factors as (x+10)(x²-4x+16), giving remaining roots 2±2√3 i. q-104514 factors as (x+2)(x²-6x+10), giving -2 and 3±i. q-104516 factors as (x-4)(x²+10x+29), giving 4 and -5±2i. q-72934 becomes (x-2)²/4+(y+2)²=1, so the full axis lengths are 4 and 2. q-71116 has altitude |WY×WZ|/|WY|=3√2/√3=√6. q-128008 has altitude |PQ×PR|/|PQ|=6√2/√19=6√38/19. q-142436 has x'=3cos(2θ), y'=3sin(2θ), so dy/dx=tan(2θ) wherever x'≠0. q-141051 has x'=3cos(2θ)-2sin(θ) and y'=3sin(2θ)+2cos(θ), so a=2, b=-2 and a-b=4. q-75295 gives y''=csc²(θ)/(-2sin(θ))=-csc³(θ)/2 wherever defined. With Euler step size 1, q-117952 produces y-values 1,2,5,26; q-120911 produces 1,1,2,2+2√2. No earlier submitted answer or revealed grade was supplied; each MA attribution below rests on its captured worked solution.",
